# Realm Suppression — Spirit Awakening Summary

When a Spirit Awakener suppresses to a lower effective CL:

- use the suppressed Proficiency Bonus where the universal Realm Suppression rule requires it;
- reduce dependent Path, Subpath, Domain, possession, and spirit-effect Source CL to the suppressed effective CL;
- do not activate or benefit from Path or Subpath features whose minimum CL exceeds the suppressed CL;
- use lower-CL scaling where a lower version exists;
- Domain Manifestation ends if effective CL falls below 15;
- a core Soul Fragment returns safely if effective CL falls below 17, unless another effect violently severed it;
- Astral Projection ends if effective CL falls below 7;
- the cultivated structure of a Soul Vessel remains, but Vessel Ward and other expressions above the suppressed CL become dormant.

Realm Suppression does not reduce or erase:

- Hit Points or Hit Dice;
- maximum Resonance;
- the existence of the Soul Anchor;
- ordinary memories, personality, identity, ancestry, relationships, oaths, or consent;
- passive Foundation quality;
- an independent spirit’s statistics unless its Source Rule scales directly from the suppressed cultivator;
- a Bond, Offering, Taboo, debt, injury, Spirit Scar, possession, custody, or consequence already created.

Suppression does not itself exorcise, sever, expel, destroy, free, or transfer a spirit. An active effect you can no longer maintain ends or becomes dormant as its Source Rule states. If the rule does not state where a Hosted or possessing spirit goes when suppressed, use the Spirit Awakening Rules Reference rather than inventing a destination.

Realm Suppression cannot refund Resonance, erase setup requirements, avoid a Bond crisis, or make an existing consequence count as lower authority after the fact.

